        "transcriptHtml": "<p class=\"transcript-note\">Automatic transcript. It may contain small recognition errors; the answer key is authoritative.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:00]</span> Section 1, you will hear a conversation between a man and a woman as they discuss a holiday. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5. Now the full test will begin. You should answer the questions as you listen, as the recording is not played twice.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:31]</span> Listen carefully to the conversation and answer questions 1 to 5. Good morning. My name is Keith Waters. I&#x27;m interested in finding out about certain type of holiday.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:42]</span> Would you be able to help me with that? Welcome to Sunshine Tours Agency. My name&#x27;s Penny. Yes, I&#x27;m sure I can help you with that.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:50]</span> What exactly are you thinking about? My wife and I are interested in a cruise of the Mediterranean. That&#x27;s a nice idea. A cruise on a ship in the Mediterranean is very popular right now.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:00]</span> Can I take some basic details from you first so I can work out what kind of cruise might suit you? Of course. So your name is Keith Waters and your wife&#x27;s?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:10]</span> Her name is Melissa Waters. Would you spell Melissa for me? It&#x27;s M-E-L-I-S-S-A. And it&#x27;s just you and your wife?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:19]</span> That&#x27;s right. We don&#x27;t have any children. Okay. Let me make a note of that.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:23]</span> Fine. Now how old are you both? I&#x27;m 32 and my wife&#x27;s 30. Thank you.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:28]</span> Now I&#x27;d like to ask about your interests and hobbies. This will help in choosing the right cruise for you. We&#x27;re both keen on traveling, of course. That&#x27;s why we&#x27;d like to go on a cruise.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:38]</span> We&#x27;re also quite sporty. We both swim in jog quite a lot. We&#x27;re interested in cinema and history. Melissa is also a keen fiction reader but I prefer non-fiction.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:47]</span> What kind of budget were you thinking about? We can spend between $7,000 and $11,000 on the trip as cheap as possible of course is best. Right.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:57]</span> I&#x27;ve got all that down. Now, I need to know when you&#x27;d like to go on your cruise and for how long? Your holiday window starts on the 1st of July and ends on the 16th of July. Okay.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:08]</span> And as for length, we&#x27;d like to have at least 14 nights on the ship. Thank you. I&#x27;m sure that&#x27;ll be possible. Before the conversation continues, you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:40]</span> Now listen carefully and answer questions 6 to 10. Right. I&#x27;ve got all that down and I&#x27;ve got some ideas for you. I&#x27;ll just make some notes while I listen.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:50]</span> If that&#x27;s all right. Of course. So, we have two boats that fit the dates you want. They sail on different dates so that gives you some flexibility.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:01]</span> First of all, I&#x27;d like to suggest the cruise on the boat the Maria Cristina. It&#x27;s a Spanish boat and you fly to Barcelona to join her. The cruise from there costs $10,500 for both of you, although the flights to get to Barcelona will be extra.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:18]</span> With that, you have all food and drinks free during the voyage. You get an inside cabin, which means that you don&#x27;t get a sea view, but you can upgrade to a sea view for further $800. They have a cinema on board with different films every night, and there are also lectures</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:35]</span> on the places where you will be visiting. There are also classes that you can do, for example, painting, cooking, art appreciation and others. That&#x27;s just in our budget, but an upgrade would put us over.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:47]</span> Yes, you&#x27;d have to do without the upgrade. Travel insurance is incorporated within the price, though. What about the next one? That&#x27;s the Sea Queen.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:56]</span> This is also a Spanish boat, but it sails from Marseilles in France and follows the same route as the Maria Cristina. Barcelona is the last stop before arriving back in Marseilles. This costs $9,000 for both of you, but this includes the return flights to Marseilles.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:14]</span> With this package, you do get a sea view, and food is inclusive throughout the voyage. All drinks excluding water are extra, though. There are fewer things going on. There is a cinema, but there are no lectures or classes.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:28]</span> There is a swimming pool and gym, though, so you&#x27;ll be able to keep up with your exercise. That&#x27;s quite a lot of information, so I&#x27;d better get back and speak to my wife. She can come back here with me in two days, so I&#x27;ll expect we&#x27;ll have chosen which boat to go on by then.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:42]</span> We can talk for the details when we come in then. That&#x27;s great. See you in two days. Yes.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:47]</span> See you soon. That is the end of section one. You will now have half a minute to check your answers. Now turn to section two.</p>"
